{
  "slug": "netlify",
  "name": "Netlify",
  "description": "Let your AI check and run your Netlify sites: sites, deploys and builds, functions, forms and submissions, environment variable names and DNS, and start builds, publish or roll back deploys and lock auto publishing after you confirm.",
  "instructions": "## Netlify\nThis connector works with Netlify through the **Netlify API** (`https://api.netlify.com/api/v1`): teams, sites, deploys and builds, build hooks, functions, forms and their submissions, environment variable names and Netlify DNS. It can start builds, publish an earlier deploy, roll back, lock or unlock auto publishing and cancel deploys after you confirm. It acts as the user who owns the token.\n\n**Setup (about 2 minutes)**\n1. In Netlify open **User settings > Applications > Personal access tokens** (https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens) and click **New access token**.\n2. Give it a description and an expiration, copy it and paste it into `NETLIFY_TOKEN`. It is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` to api.netlify.com only.\n3. Check the setup with `netlify_get_current_user`, then `netlify_list_sites`.\n\nA personal access token has the user's full rights in every team they belong to; Netlify has no read-only tokens. Share the MCP server only with people allowed to deploy, and switch off the write tools for a read-only setup.\n\n**How to work**\n1. `netlify_list_accounts` lists your teams; `netlify_list_sites` gives each site's id (a site's domain such as my-site.netlify.app works as site_id too).\n2. Deploys: `netlify_list_deploys` (filter by branch, state or production), `netlify_get_deploy`; builds: `netlify_list_builds`, `netlify_get_build`, `netlify_list_build_hooks`.\n3. Site details: `netlify_get_site`, `netlify_list_functions`, `netlify_list_env_vars`.\n4. Forms: `netlify_list_forms`, then `netlify_list_form_submissions`. Submissions hold what visitors typed, often personal data.\n5. DNS: `netlify_list_dns_zones`, then `netlify_list_dns_records` (only for domains on Netlify DNS).\n\n**Writes always need the user's confirmation**: `netlify_trigger_build` (also the way to retry a failed deploy; a production build publishes when it succeeds), `netlify_restore_deploy` and `netlify_rollback_site` (change what visitors see immediately), `netlify_lock_deploy`, `netlify_unlock_deploy` and `netlify_cancel_deploy`. Say what will change and call only after the user agrees.\n\n**Secrets**: `netlify_list_env_vars` returns names, scopes and contexts, never values. `netlify_get_env_var_value` is installed switched off: it returns non-secret values in plain text (secret ones stay masked). Turn it on only if the AI really needs a value. Build hook URLs, site passwords and deploy hook URLs are never returned.\n\n**Switched off at install**: `netlify_delete_form_submission` and `netlify_get_env_var_value`.\n\n**Pagination**: lists with page and per_page carry `_pagination` when there is another page; call again with page = `_pagination.nextCursor` until it is absent.\n\n**Errors**: 401 means the token is wrong, expired or revoked. 403 means the user lacks the role for this team or site. 404 means a wrong site, deploy or form id, or one the user cannot see. 422 names an invalid value. 429 means the rate limit is reached (about 500 requests a minute, and only a few deploys a minute); wait and retry.\n\n**Out of scope here**: creating, deleting or configuring sites, uploading files, editing environment variables, DNS records or domains, and site analytics, which Netlify does not offer in its public API.",
  "region": "intl",
  "category": "infrastructure",
  "icon": "netlify",
  "docsUrl": "https://open-api.netlify.com/",
  "prerequisites": "A Netlify account with access to the sites, and a personal access token from User settings > Applications. About 2 minutes.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "NETLIFY_TOKEN"
  ],
  "appRegistrationUrl": "https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens",
  "envVarMeta": {
    "NETLIFY_TOKEN": {
      "label": "Personal access token",
      "kind": "credential",
      "secret": true,
      "help": "Netlify, User settings, Applications, Personal access tokens, New access token. Paste only the token, without Bearer.",
      "link": "https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens",
      "example": "nfp_...",
      "pattern": "^(?!Bearer\\s)\\S{20,}$",
      "patternMessage": "Paste only the personal access token (newer ones start with nfp_), without spaces or the word Bearer."
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Netlify refused the token: it is wrong, expired or revoked. Create a new personal access token under User settings, Applications.",
    "403": "The token works but the user lacks the role for this team or site.",
    "rate_limited": "Netlify is rate limiting this token. Wait a minute and verify again."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "netlify_get_current_user"
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Netlify API",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.netlify.com/api/v1",
    "authType": "BEARER_TOKEN",
    "authConfig": {
      "token": "{{NETLIFY_TOKEN}}"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json",
      "User-Agent": "AnythingMCP"
    },
    "healthcheckPath": "/user"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "netlify_get_current_user",
      "description": "Get the Netlify user the personal access token belongs to: id, name, email, number of sites and last login. A quick check that the token works. Read-only.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/user"
      },
      "responseMapping": {
        "transform": {
          "select": {
            "id": "$.id",
            "full_name": "$.full_name",
            "email": "$.email",
            "site_count": "$.site_count",
            "created_at": "$.created_at",
            "last_login": "$.last_login"
          }
        }
      }
    },
